#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is inspired by and based upon research conducted at Cleveland Clinic, as described in [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), exposing the full workflow for implicit solvent calculations and extending it with iterative solvent self-consistency (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), geometry optimization, and automatic qubit layout selection. Please refer to the [SQD IEF-PCM Qiskit Function template](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), jointly developed by Cleveland Clinic and IBM&reg; based on Cleveland Clinic research, for a streamlined, black-box interface for running implicit solvent calculations.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini terinspirasi dan didasarkan pada riset yang dilakukan di Cleveland Clinic, seperti yang dijelaskan dalam [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), yang memaparkan alur kerja lengkap untuk perhitungan pelarut implisit dan memperluasnya dengan self-consistency pelarut iteratif (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), optimasi geometri, dan pemilihan tata letak qubit otomatis. Silakan lihat [SQD IEF-PCM Qiskit Function template](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), yang dikembangkan bersama oleh Cleveland Clinic dan IBM&reg; berdasarkan riset Cleveland Clinic, untuk antarmuka black-box yang efisien untuk menjalankan perhitungan pelarut implisit.\n"

